1
00:00:50,564 --> 00:00:53,859
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

2
00:00:54,568 --> 00:00:55,777
Ms. Da-reum.

3
00:00:56,319 --> 00:00:58,196
I'm not into men.

4
00:00:58,947 --> 00:01:00,198
- What?
- Also...

5
00:01:02,033 --> 00:01:03,827
there's this woman
I'm interested in right now.

6
00:01:05,620 --> 00:01:06,663
What?

7
00:01:38,236 --> 00:01:39,279
Director Lee.

8
00:01:39,821 --> 00:01:40,906
How did you find us here?

9
00:01:51,708 --> 00:01:52,876
I heard about the covert op.

10
00:01:53,793 --> 00:01:56,671
Ms. Kim told me that you had trouble
trying to get Master Im on board.

11
00:01:57,255 --> 00:01:58,340
I came out to help.

12
00:01:59,132 --> 00:02:00,133
At this hour?

13
00:02:00,675 --> 00:02:01,718
Did you really come for work?

14
00:02:01,801 --> 00:02:04,596
Of course.
I'm that serious about work.

15
00:02:11,102 --> 00:02:12,145
So, well...

16
00:02:12,771 --> 00:02:14,773
There are only two rooms.

17
00:02:14,981 --> 00:02:16,399
I can crash in his room.

18
00:02:17,400 --> 00:02:19,694
- You, in my room?
- It's not like I can take her room.

19
00:02:21,947 --> 00:02:23,949
Well, that wasn't what I meant.

20
00:02:24,199 --> 00:02:26,159
It's nothing new between us.

21
00:02:30,580 --> 00:02:31,665
Get away from me.

22
00:02:35,377 --> 00:02:37,921
I won't misunderstand
the situation anymore, Mr. Kang.

23
00:02:38,004 --> 00:02:39,005
Don't worry.

24
00:02:39,548 --> 00:02:40,549
"Misunderstand"?

25
00:02:40,966 --> 00:02:43,260
Well, if it's
too inconvenient for you

26
00:02:43,343 --> 00:02:45,637
I can sleep out in the hall.

27
00:02:45,971 --> 00:02:48,306
No, you should take one of the rooms.

28
00:02:48,682 --> 00:02:50,433
- I'll share mine with him.
- Okay.

29
00:02:51,142 --> 00:02:52,519
Okay. Then it's decided.

30
00:02:52,769 --> 00:02:53,812
We'll take this one.

31
00:02:55,397 --> 00:02:58,400
- Good night.
- Have a good rest.

32
00:03:13,248 --> 00:03:15,417
You have a thing
for Director Lee Chan.

33
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:18,211
For a long time.

34
00:03:20,755 --> 00:03:21,798
I mean, me?

35
00:03:23,466 --> 00:03:25,635
- Jeez.
- Da-reum is unbelievable.

36
00:03:25,719 --> 00:03:28,346
What about me gives off that vibe?

37
00:03:34,894 --> 00:03:36,438
Are you disappointed

38
00:03:36,688 --> 00:03:37,939
that she doesn't think of you
as a man?

39
00:03:38,023 --> 00:03:39,024
Whatever.

40
00:03:39,899 --> 00:03:40,900
Gosh.

41
00:03:46,781 --> 00:03:47,782
I can tell

42
00:03:49,326 --> 00:03:50,910
that you care about Da-reum.

43
00:03:52,370 --> 00:03:53,705
Concerned? Hardly.

44
00:03:55,582 --> 00:03:57,125
She's new to work.

45
00:03:57,208 --> 00:03:58,501
That's why I'm looking out for her.

46
00:04:02,922 --> 00:04:05,550
Looking out for someone and actually
caring for them aren't the same.

47
00:04:07,302 --> 00:04:08,386
It's different.

48
00:04:20,273 --> 00:04:21,608
Wait, Ms. Nam.

49
00:04:23,860 --> 00:04:25,487
- What?
- Also...

50
00:04:26,363 --> 00:04:28,073
there's this woman
I'm interested in right now.

51
00:04:30,408 --> 00:04:31,409
What?

52
00:04:46,216 --> 00:04:48,259
I could see today
that you two have grown close.

53
00:04:49,302 --> 00:04:52,013
I had a feeling
that you might be interested in her.

54
00:04:54,808 --> 00:04:55,809
I'm not.

55
00:04:57,060 --> 00:04:58,103
Even if I did

56
00:04:59,062 --> 00:05:00,897
it's impossible for a CEO
to date a rookie.

57
00:05:22,794 --> 00:05:25,547
So Mr. Kang wasn't into men.

58
00:05:27,298 --> 00:05:30,385
Who's the woman he's interested in?

59
00:05:39,686 --> 00:05:40,854
Come on, Da-reum.

60
00:05:41,396 --> 00:05:44,482
Why do you want to know that?

61
00:05:44,899 --> 00:05:46,025
Come on.

62
00:05:48,403 --> 00:05:51,072
Could it be someone at work?

63
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,951
Yes, just like that.

64
00:06:37,035 --> 00:06:38,077
Don't let it get tangled.

65
00:06:38,161 --> 00:06:39,913
Like that.

66
00:06:39,996 --> 00:06:42,081
That's it. Carefully.

67
00:06:42,165 --> 00:06:43,541
Okay. Good.

68
00:06:46,586 --> 00:06:47,670
You have a knack for this.

69
00:06:52,842 --> 00:06:54,385
Did you have trouble sleeping too?

70
00:06:55,970 --> 00:06:57,013
Yes.

71
00:06:57,722 --> 00:06:59,265
And I saw the light was on.

72
00:07:00,850 --> 00:07:02,143
Come here and join me.

73
00:07:04,771 --> 00:07:05,772
May I?

74
00:07:09,108 --> 00:07:11,945
It's best to move your hands
when you're stressed out.

75
00:07:12,570 --> 00:07:14,447
Knotting may seem like a job
where you tie things

76
00:07:14,531 --> 00:07:17,408
but you'll come to learn
that it can untangle your heart.

77
00:07:18,576 --> 00:07:21,579
You're right.
Tying knots helped me clear my head.

78
00:07:23,748 --> 00:07:25,875
- You should give it a go too.
- Okay.

79
00:07:26,125 --> 00:07:27,919
- Do what you did yesterday.
- Okay.

80
00:07:35,718 --> 00:07:38,429
I let my feelings
get ahead of me yesterday.

81
00:07:38,930 --> 00:07:40,515
I shouldn't have said it like that.

82
00:07:42,892 --> 00:07:45,603
So even if Master Im
doesn't agree to be on board

83
00:07:46,062 --> 00:07:49,107
I hope you two can make
these traditional knots more visible.

84
00:07:51,484 --> 00:07:54,153
We completely understand
what you mean.

85
00:07:55,822 --> 00:07:58,867
I'm happy to know that you do.

86
00:08:00,368 --> 00:08:02,662
Please continue to practice.
I'll get breakfast ready.

87
00:08:03,037 --> 00:08:04,706
- Sure.
- And this one.

88
00:08:05,081 --> 00:08:06,541
I'm taking your first knot.

89
00:08:12,755 --> 00:08:15,258
Ta-da. I made a new one.

90
00:08:15,508 --> 00:08:16,843
I learned it just now.

91
00:08:16,926 --> 00:08:19,095
- You've learned it already?
- Yes.

92
00:08:20,054 --> 00:08:22,098
Do you want me to teach you?

93
00:08:22,724 --> 00:08:23,766
Sure.

94
00:08:24,183 --> 00:08:25,226
Let's do it.

95
00:08:26,102 --> 00:08:28,187
All right. Take a good look.

96
00:08:28,730 --> 00:08:31,482
Put the green cord
on top of the pink one

97
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:33,860
and create a knot.

98
00:08:34,485 --> 00:08:37,697
Good. Now do you see this space here?

99
00:08:37,780 --> 00:08:39,574
Spread it out a little.

100
00:08:39,657 --> 00:08:41,576
Look, it's a heart.

101
00:08:43,870 --> 00:08:49,125
Then hold the top
and make a wing on each side.

102
00:08:49,834 --> 00:08:51,920
- A wing...
- Yes.

103
00:08:53,212 --> 00:08:56,507
Then hold the top
and pull it to the side.

104
00:09:20,198 --> 00:09:23,284
The young lady
who came from Seoul made this.

105
00:09:24,661 --> 00:09:26,079
She tried rather hard

106
00:09:26,788 --> 00:09:27,872
after just one day.

107
00:09:34,963 --> 00:09:36,422
Isn't that admirable?

108
00:09:41,886 --> 00:09:42,887
Master Im.

109
00:09:44,097 --> 00:09:46,391
I apologize for yesterday.

110
00:09:47,767 --> 00:09:50,019
I knew your intentions very well.

111
00:09:54,148 --> 00:09:55,733
It's always tough

112
00:09:57,193 --> 00:09:58,486
to be a teacher.

113
00:09:59,070 --> 00:10:01,781
I must always keep an eye
on people's feelings as I proceed...

114
00:10:04,742 --> 00:10:06,202
but at times,
I find myself blurting out words

115
00:10:07,412 --> 00:10:08,871
that can turn into sharp blades.

116
00:10:12,125 --> 00:10:13,209
Are you

117
00:10:13,835 --> 00:10:15,420
apologizing right now?

118
00:10:25,013 --> 00:10:27,306
I was just afraid.

119
00:10:28,141 --> 00:10:32,311
That everything we have stood for
would disappear down that road.

120
00:10:40,403 --> 00:10:42,530
It won't disappear, Master Im.

121
00:11:13,311 --> 00:11:14,562
How beautiful.

122
00:11:16,898 --> 00:11:18,107
These are so pretty.

123
00:11:21,027 --> 00:11:22,528
When did you come out?

124
00:11:24,072 --> 00:11:25,073
Just now.

125
00:11:25,740 --> 00:11:28,284
They looked so pretty from the window

126
00:11:28,826 --> 00:11:30,244
so I came out to see them up close.

127
00:11:46,594 --> 00:11:49,055
I'm sorry for that day.

128
00:11:51,182 --> 00:11:54,852
It had been weighing on my mind
after you left like that.

129
00:11:59,148 --> 00:12:00,233
Please don't mind me.

130
00:12:00,983 --> 00:12:03,569
You suffered from a misunderstanding
because of me.

131
00:12:04,028 --> 00:12:05,238
It must've put you in a tough spot.

132
00:12:06,823 --> 00:12:08,491
She and I had already broken up.

133
00:12:09,867 --> 00:12:11,202
She must've said

134
00:12:11,869 --> 00:12:14,163
all those mean things to you
out of spite for me.

135
00:12:15,665 --> 00:12:16,791
I apologize.

136
00:12:20,002 --> 00:12:21,796
I'm really fine.

137
00:12:28,094 --> 00:12:30,012
I'm okay, really.

138
00:12:37,103 --> 00:12:38,146
Da-reum.

139
00:12:38,479 --> 00:12:40,398
There's something I want to show you.

140
00:12:41,816 --> 00:12:45,111
Can you spare me some time
on our way back to Seoul?

141
00:12:55,496 --> 00:12:57,039
A lot went through my mind

142
00:12:57,957 --> 00:12:59,417
after learning how to make knots.

143
00:13:00,334 --> 00:13:02,587
Traditional knots
are a form of art and meditation

144
00:13:02,795 --> 00:13:04,755
not something
you can print with a machine.

145
00:13:05,464 --> 00:13:07,592
I brought up words
like factory production

146
00:13:07,675 --> 00:13:09,468
without realizing
how deep the practice was.

147
00:13:12,263 --> 00:13:13,264
I apologize.

148
00:13:14,015 --> 00:13:15,308
I apologize.

149
00:13:16,601 --> 00:13:18,436
And because we desperately
wanted to work with you

150
00:13:18,936 --> 00:13:20,813
I also had forgotten
about the core of my business.

151
00:13:21,439 --> 00:13:23,524
Appello strives
to maintain value that will last

152
00:13:24,650 --> 00:13:26,444
instead of fast-paced trends.

153
00:13:28,112 --> 00:13:30,239
So what if we provided
an experience for the people

154
00:13:30,656 --> 00:13:33,618
in the exact traditional way
of your practice?

155
00:13:42,835 --> 00:13:46,172
How about putting together a DIY kit

156
00:13:46,255 --> 00:13:48,049
so people can try making
traditional Korean knots

157
00:13:48,132 --> 00:13:51,552
with all the materials
and instructions at home?

158
00:13:52,553 --> 00:13:55,056
I thought
it was very difficult to make knots

159
00:13:55,139 --> 00:13:57,391
but I had so much fun
when I got my hands on it.

160
00:13:57,725 --> 00:14:00,019
I'm sure many people will love it.

161
00:14:10,238 --> 00:14:11,948
Perhaps it's more meaningful

162
00:14:13,115 --> 00:14:15,910
to have knots
created by many new hands

163
00:14:18,412 --> 00:14:21,332
instead of ones made
by a single artisan.

164
00:14:23,125 --> 00:14:26,212
If you're going to make it,
make it right.

165
00:14:26,712 --> 00:14:28,172
The traditional knot kit.

166
00:14:30,967 --> 00:14:32,093
Thank you, Master Im.

167
00:14:32,176 --> 00:14:34,428
- Thank you, ma'am.
- However...

168
00:14:35,388 --> 00:14:36,597
there is one condition.

169
00:14:37,306 --> 00:14:40,893
I won't allow you to make something
with half-hearted instructions.

170
00:14:41,143 --> 00:14:42,853
They must have hands-on experience

171
00:14:44,063 --> 00:14:46,023
as they learn to make actual knots.

172
00:14:47,358 --> 00:14:50,236
Do you mean that people must
take part in the experience?

173
00:14:50,945 --> 00:14:52,530
That's what will actually last.

174
00:14:53,239 --> 00:14:54,782
I'll see what you come up with

175
00:14:54,865 --> 00:14:57,368
before I go ahead
and give you my final approval.

176
00:15:14,135 --> 00:15:16,512
- Hop in, Ms. Nam.
- Okay.

177
00:15:17,096 --> 00:15:18,931
Ms. Da-reum, let's go in my car.

178
00:15:20,057 --> 00:15:21,392
You'd probably prefer to go alone.

179
00:15:22,435 --> 00:15:24,812
Come with me. His car
isn't built for long-distance trips.

180
00:15:25,646 --> 00:15:28,691
What do you mean?
I'd get there an hour before you.

181
00:15:30,276 --> 00:15:31,319
Hey.

182
00:15:32,028 --> 00:15:33,904
My seats come with a massager.

183
00:15:35,531 --> 00:15:37,408
You can lie down flat on my seat.

184
00:15:43,956 --> 00:15:45,291
Ms. Da-reum,
whose car do you want to take?

185
00:15:48,669 --> 00:15:50,963
First of all,
can you let my hands go?

186
00:15:57,762 --> 00:15:58,804
Then...

187
00:16:01,140 --> 00:16:02,892
I'm sorry for that day.

188
00:16:03,601 --> 00:16:05,728
There's something I want to show you.

189
00:16:05,853 --> 00:16:07,271
Can you spare me some time

190
00:16:07,813 --> 00:16:09,315
on our way back to Seoul?

191
00:16:13,194 --> 00:16:14,445
May I take

192
00:16:14,987 --> 00:16:16,864
Director Lee's car?

193
00:16:16,947 --> 00:16:18,574
You'll also find
that more convenient.

194
00:16:21,118 --> 00:16:22,203
All right, then.

195
00:16:25,456 --> 00:16:26,874
Was my car uncomfortable?

196
00:16:28,501 --> 00:16:31,712
No, it was such a comfortable ride.

197
00:16:31,796 --> 00:16:35,091
I just felt bad
that you always had to give me rides.

198
00:16:38,469 --> 00:16:40,721
I'll take Ms. Da-reum home.

199
00:16:44,350 --> 00:16:45,684
Have a safe trip back.

200
00:16:47,770 --> 00:16:48,979
Thank you.

201
00:16:54,652 --> 00:16:55,736
Hey, Ha-gi.

202
00:16:56,779 --> 00:16:57,863
Drive safely.

203
00:16:58,447 --> 00:16:59,532
Sure.

204
00:17:12,294 --> 00:17:13,629
Do you know where you are?

205
00:17:16,674 --> 00:17:19,760
It's a bus stop in my neighborhood.

206
00:17:27,184 --> 00:17:28,978
D.N.X FOREVER
LET'S STAY TOGETHER FOREVER

207
00:17:29,228 --> 00:17:30,479
Oh, this...

208
00:17:31,730 --> 00:17:32,898
You wrote this.

209
00:17:34,150 --> 00:17:35,609
How did you know that?

210
00:17:39,572 --> 00:17:40,823
Do you remember this photo book?

211
00:17:43,701 --> 00:17:45,244
This is...

212
00:17:58,340 --> 00:17:59,425
Chan.

213
00:18:03,971 --> 00:18:05,764
EXCLUSIVE:
WHERE IS D.N.X'S LEE CHAN NOW?

214
00:18:08,601 --> 00:18:09,852
DISAPPEARED AFTER THEY DISBANDED

215
00:18:09,935 --> 00:18:11,061
D.N.X DISBANDS AFTER 3 YEARS

216
00:18:16,275 --> 00:18:17,776
I can't believe D.N.X still has fans.

217
00:18:18,277 --> 00:18:19,778
I thought they were over.

218
00:18:19,862 --> 00:18:22,448
- Be quiet.
- I'm not wrong.

219
00:18:22,531 --> 00:18:24,158
I feel bad for her.

220
00:18:24,825 --> 00:18:26,035
It must be embarrassing.

221
00:18:44,220 --> 00:18:46,805
D.N.X FOREVER
WE WILL BE TOGETHER FOREVER

222
00:18:46,889 --> 00:18:49,225
"DESTINY NEVER X,"
I KNOW I'LL SEE YOU ON STAGE AGAIN

223
00:18:54,522 --> 00:18:56,982
I can't believe you still had this.

224
00:18:58,025 --> 00:19:00,152
When I was going through
the toughest time after we disbanded

225
00:19:01,153 --> 00:19:03,280
this journal helped me stay strong.

226
00:19:08,869 --> 00:19:12,706
I didn't expect you
to hold this so dearly.

227
00:19:14,500 --> 00:19:17,795
During those toughest days,
I went and looked for these places.

228
00:19:21,966 --> 00:19:23,467
I thought I'd perhaps see you.

229
00:19:34,645 --> 00:19:35,980
D.N.X FOREVER
LET'S STAY TOGETHER FOREVER

230
00:19:38,190 --> 00:19:40,943
D.N.X FOREVER
LET'S STAY TOGETHER FOREVER

231
00:19:54,373 --> 00:19:55,499
The person who continued

232
00:19:56,458 --> 00:19:58,085
to show me their support somewhere.

233
00:20:02,298 --> 00:20:03,591
And now, we've finally met.

234
00:20:12,474 --> 00:20:14,518
This is fascinating.

235
00:20:16,687 --> 00:20:19,356
I also spent
a lot of time sitting here

236
00:20:19,857 --> 00:20:21,567
listening to your songs

237
00:20:21,984 --> 00:20:23,736
just trying to get through life.

238
00:20:31,827 --> 00:20:32,828
We have

239
00:20:33,537 --> 00:20:36,081
always been supporting each other
from a distance, right?

240
00:20:39,877 --> 00:20:41,003
How about...

241
00:20:43,213 --> 00:20:44,423
we stay by each other's side

242
00:20:45,090 --> 00:20:46,508
from now on?

243
00:20:50,596 --> 00:20:51,597
Sorry?

244
00:20:56,310 --> 00:20:58,187
I want to start dating you.

245
00:20:58,812 --> 00:20:59,813
Da-reum.

246
00:21:03,692 --> 00:21:04,693
I want

247
00:21:06,153 --> 00:21:07,321
to get to know you more.

248
00:21:25,422 --> 00:21:26,924
I thought you were
hitting it off with the CEO.

249
00:21:27,007 --> 00:21:28,467
What's this plot twist?

250
00:21:28,550 --> 00:21:32,179
Did Chan really ask you out first?

251
00:21:34,139 --> 00:21:35,140
Yes.

252
00:21:40,020 --> 00:21:42,481
No way.
This is straight out of Notting Hill.

253
00:21:43,941 --> 00:21:46,527
I can't believe Chan is
Namda's first potential boyfriend.

254
00:21:47,236 --> 00:21:51,031
This is why you should
never give up on something.

255
00:21:51,115 --> 00:21:53,409
So? What did you say to him?

256
00:21:56,161 --> 00:21:57,579
I haven't said anything.

257
00:21:57,830 --> 00:21:58,914
I'm still thinking about it.

258
00:21:59,581 --> 00:22:02,042
You're thinking?
Why would you do that?

259
00:22:03,001 --> 00:22:05,963
I also want to know
what he's really like

260
00:22:06,130 --> 00:22:08,799
not as a celebrity,
but a real person.

261
00:22:09,967 --> 00:22:14,096
But if I rushed into this,
I might ruin all my great memories.

262
00:22:15,806 --> 00:22:18,142
I got a bit scared.

263
00:22:26,024 --> 00:22:28,360
Try going on three dates.

264
00:22:31,864 --> 00:22:33,907
It's not something
you can conclude by thinking.

265
00:22:36,869 --> 00:22:37,995
You should

266
