00:40:04,749 --> 00:40:06,125
I got a muscle cramp.

531
00:40:07,668 --> 00:40:08,878
Maybe you were too immersed.

532
00:40:19,347 --> 00:40:20,598
Oh, Chan.

533
00:40:20,890 --> 00:40:22,975
What about the knot?
Have you had a chance to practice?

534
00:40:23,309 --> 00:40:24,310
Of course.

535
00:40:24,769 --> 00:40:26,771
I practiced it like five times today
every time I had a chance.

536
00:40:26,854 --> 00:40:28,356
What? Really?

537
00:40:30,024 --> 00:40:33,653
What? Are you worried
that I might ruin your first project?

538
00:40:33,736 --> 00:40:35,571
Yes. I'd better check.

539
00:40:36,864 --> 00:40:37,949
When?

540
00:40:38,407 --> 00:40:40,493
No, I was just joking.

541
00:40:43,287 --> 00:40:44,455
It's a cat.

542
00:40:54,674 --> 00:40:56,467
He must be cold.

543
00:40:56,884 --> 00:40:57,885
I know.

544
00:40:59,262 --> 00:41:01,430
He's cute. He's still a baby.

545
00:41:03,349 --> 00:41:04,559
They're kittens.

546
00:41:04,934 --> 00:41:06,686
I can't just leave them here.

547
00:41:06,811 --> 00:41:08,771
Then I'll keep them for now.

548
00:41:15,403 --> 00:41:16,654
- What's wrong?
- What?

549
00:41:19,615 --> 00:41:21,367
He reminds me of a cat I know.

550
00:41:24,245 --> 00:41:25,288
Hi.

551
00:41:28,875 --> 00:41:30,626
Do you want to grab something hot
over there?

552
00:41:31,294 --> 00:41:32,712
Oh, yes.

553
00:41:44,307 --> 00:41:46,475
They requested a change
to the contract terms

554
00:41:46,559 --> 00:41:48,561
but it's difficult for us
to accept it.

555
00:41:48,644 --> 00:41:50,187
I'll persuade them myself in person.

556
00:41:50,271 --> 00:41:52,273
Please check
the investor's schedule again.

557
00:41:52,356 --> 00:41:53,357
Okay, Mr. Kang.

558
00:42:00,990 --> 00:42:02,325
This is obstruction of business.

559
00:42:03,451 --> 00:42:04,577
Is it warm here?

560
00:42:14,670 --> 00:42:16,005
About your owner

561
00:42:16,589 --> 00:42:17,882
who did she go meet?

562
00:42:20,092 --> 00:42:21,260
She's taking so long.

563
00:42:28,851 --> 00:42:30,645
- Soybean milk?
- Sounds good.

564
00:42:32,438 --> 00:42:33,481
It's warm.

565
00:42:35,524 --> 00:42:39,403
Excuse me. Aren't you Lee Chan?

566
00:42:39,946 --> 00:42:41,572
- I...
- Right?

567
00:42:42,073 --> 00:42:43,741
I'm a big fan of yours.

568
00:42:44,200 --> 00:42:45,993
It's really him. Awesome.

569
00:42:48,120 --> 00:42:51,248
And she's...

570
00:42:55,753 --> 00:42:56,837
I'm...

571
00:42:58,673 --> 00:43:00,174
Excuse me.

572
00:43:01,258 --> 00:43:03,177
I'm just a passerby.

573
00:43:04,887 --> 00:43:06,180
- You're so hot.
- You're so handsome.

574
00:43:06,263 --> 00:43:07,515
- Can I have a picture?
- How are you so hot?

575
00:43:07,598 --> 00:43:10,518
- You're crazy good-looking.
- My heart is going to explode.

576
00:43:10,601 --> 00:43:12,019
You're unbelievably hot.

577
00:43:12,103 --> 00:43:14,563
Oh, my heart is going to explode.
Let me join.

578
00:43:15,189 --> 00:43:16,399
This is crazy.

579
00:43:29,203 --> 00:43:32,581
His life must be tough.

580
00:43:39,088 --> 00:43:40,131
Gosh, it's cold.

581
00:43:47,638 --> 00:43:49,140
It is him. He's still there.

582
00:43:49,890 --> 00:43:51,058
Awesome.

583
00:43:51,225 --> 00:43:53,019
What a treat to see
Chan in his plain clothes.

584
00:43:53,227 --> 00:43:54,437
But is he alone?

585
00:43:54,645 --> 00:43:56,647
I heard he was seen with someone
in the theater.

586
00:43:56,731 --> 00:43:58,149
- With whom?
- A woman.

587
00:43:58,399 --> 00:43:59,984
If I get in the picture with him

588
00:44:00,317 --> 00:44:01,736
that'll get him in trouble.

589
00:44:05,322 --> 00:44:06,866
Chan, can I have a selfie with you?

590
00:44:07,199 --> 00:44:09,910
- It's really him.
- He's so hot. I can't believe it.

591
00:44:09,994 --> 00:44:11,287
Don't go.

592
00:44:11,370 --> 00:44:12,872
- You're so hot.
- Excuse me. Sorry.

593
00:44:12,955 --> 00:44:14,290
Where are you going?

594
00:44:26,594 --> 00:44:27,970
He must be somewhere nearby.

595
00:44:28,262 --> 00:44:30,014
But he seemed different today.

596
00:44:30,097 --> 00:44:31,724
Didn't he look like he had company?

597
00:44:31,807 --> 00:44:34,643
- Right?
- See this? It's that place.

598
00:44:36,187 --> 00:44:39,273
Oh, how did I miss him?

599
00:44:40,900 --> 00:44:42,651
Right. Look at that.

600
00:45:09,345 --> 00:45:10,679
I barely lost them.

601
00:45:11,222 --> 00:45:12,348
Where did Da-reum go?

602
00:45:16,268 --> 00:45:17,353
DA-REUM

603
00:45:17,812 --> 00:45:21,899
Chan, I think we should
split up for today.

604
00:45:22,274 --> 00:45:24,110
Still, I had a good time.

605
00:45:24,401 --> 00:45:26,779
I have work to do.
I'll head home first.

606
00:45:42,378 --> 00:45:44,296
I feel bad
to send you home like this.

607
00:45:49,718 --> 00:45:53,180
"I'm really fine."

608
00:46:02,148 --> 00:46:04,024
Why do I keep saying I'm okay?

609
00:46:09,780 --> 00:46:11,365
I'm clearly not okay.

610
00:46:21,876 --> 00:46:24,545
CEO KANG HA-GI OF APPELLO

611
00:46:25,629 --> 00:46:26,630
Hello?

612
00:46:29,466 --> 00:46:30,968
Well...

613
00:46:32,386 --> 00:46:33,679
Ms. Da-reum.

614
00:46:33,971 --> 00:46:34,972
Are you

615
00:46:36,140 --> 00:46:37,516
still busy?

616
00:46:37,600 --> 00:46:40,102
What? Is something wrong?

617
00:46:42,980 --> 00:46:44,064
That is...

618
00:46:49,403 --> 00:46:50,863
The cats.

619
00:46:54,408 --> 00:46:57,286
One of them sleeps too much.

620
00:46:57,745 --> 00:46:59,163
I don't know much about cats.

621
00:46:59,663 --> 00:47:02,499
I thought you should look into them.

622
00:47:02,583 --> 00:47:03,667
Really?

623
00:47:04,293 --> 00:47:05,836
I'll be there soon.

624
00:47:14,678 --> 00:47:15,679
Okay.

625
00:47:16,347 --> 00:47:18,182
They were sleeping until now.

626
00:47:19,725 --> 00:47:21,685
It's not a lie.

627
00:47:34,531 --> 00:47:37,868
I'm sorry. I hope I'm not too late.

628
00:47:37,952 --> 00:47:39,286
Oh, no.

629
00:47:41,205 --> 00:47:42,665
Why do you look so cold?

630
00:47:44,333 --> 00:47:46,418
It's pretty cold.

631
00:47:49,338 --> 00:47:50,839
I hope I didn't disturb you

632
00:47:51,715 --> 00:47:52,716
when you were having fun.

633
00:47:53,217 --> 00:47:54,802
Oh, not at all.

634
00:47:55,552 --> 00:47:56,553
Where are the cats?

635
00:47:56,887 --> 00:47:57,888
Upstairs. Come with me.

636
00:48:09,608 --> 00:48:10,693
So cute.

637
00:48:15,531 --> 00:48:17,157
Drink this and warm up before you go.

638
00:48:17,241 --> 00:48:18,826
Oh, thank you.

639
00:48:24,164 --> 00:48:26,375
- Are you okay?
- Yes, thank you.

640
00:48:30,045 --> 00:48:31,505
Did they just sleep the whole time?

641
00:48:38,220 --> 00:48:39,722
After I hung up the phone

642
00:48:40,639 --> 00:48:42,850
they ate and played just fine.

643
00:48:44,435 --> 00:48:45,561
That's good.

644
00:48:46,103 --> 00:48:48,397
Thank you
for watching the kittens today.

645
00:48:49,273 --> 00:48:50,316
Don't mention it.

646
00:48:51,984 --> 00:48:54,653
They really hit it off
and seemed to have fun.

647
00:48:56,155 --> 00:48:57,281
They hit it off?

648
00:48:59,283 --> 00:49:01,243
Then I should name one Kung

649
00:49:01,327 --> 00:49:03,954
and the other one Jjak, right?

650
00:49:04,038 --> 00:49:05,914
The big one will be Jjak.

651
00:49:06,123 --> 00:49:07,291
The small one will be Kung.

652
00:49:07,958 --> 00:49:09,126
Kung and Jjak.

653
00:49:10,502 --> 00:49:11,503
That works.

654
00:49:14,423 --> 00:49:17,843
But I think you should separate them
for a while.

655
00:49:18,344 --> 00:49:21,263
- Why is that?
- Kung keeps eating Jjak's food.

656
00:49:22,431 --> 00:49:24,683
When you leave home for work,
Jjak will end up starving.

657
00:49:25,100 --> 00:49:27,603
I'll watch Kung for a while.

658
00:49:28,687 --> 00:49:29,813
Really?

659
00:49:30,981 --> 00:49:32,691
Thank you so much, Mr. Kang.

660
00:49:35,027 --> 00:49:37,404
And I've grown
attached to them already.

661
00:49:43,077 --> 00:49:45,204
Do you watch Bitter Sweet too?

662
00:49:45,579 --> 00:49:46,789
Because Director Lee is
starring in it.

663
00:49:47,331 --> 00:49:50,793
I watch them at once to see
if anything might raise an issue.

664
00:49:56,673 --> 00:49:58,675
I feel like
this is a one-sided crush.

665
00:49:58,759 --> 00:50:00,302
That's not true.

666
00:50:00,386 --> 00:50:01,637
I like you too.

667
00:50:02,262 --> 00:50:03,931
I'm just not good
at expressing myself.

668
00:50:05,140 --> 00:50:06,683
You have to say it.

669
00:50:08,894 --> 00:50:09,895
I love you.

670
00:50:13,524 --> 00:50:14,566
I love you.

671
00:50:16,318 --> 00:50:17,319
What was that?

672
00:50:18,112 --> 00:50:19,154
I love you.

673
00:50:19,613 --> 00:50:20,906
I love you, too.

674
00:50:22,324 --> 00:50:23,450
I'm jealous.

675
00:50:25,577 --> 00:50:26,620
Of what?

676
00:50:29,039 --> 00:50:31,959
She can be pouty and sullen

677
00:50:32,418 --> 00:50:33,544
in front of the person she likes.

678
00:50:34,086 --> 00:50:35,087
You are

679
00:50:36,213 --> 00:50:37,214
jealous of that?

680
00:50:39,258 --> 00:50:41,343
That shows how close they are.

681
00:50:44,721 --> 00:50:46,640
When I like someone

682
00:50:46,974 --> 00:50:49,351
I tend to keep it to myself.

683
00:50:49,977 --> 00:50:53,814
But sometimes
I wish I could show how I feel.

684
00:51:06,118 --> 00:51:07,369
Wanting that much

685
00:51:08,787 --> 00:51:10,247
sounds like
a very healthy relationship.

686
00:51:12,291 --> 00:51:13,292
Right?

687
00:51:16,795 --> 00:51:18,088
I'm sorry, Ms. Da-reum.

688
00:51:18,797 --> 00:51:20,174
I can't accept your heart.

689
00:51:20,841 --> 00:51:21,842
If only

690
00:51:22,718 --> 00:51:24,219
I hadn't been a CEO.

691
00:51:26,388 --> 00:51:28,307
No, Kang Ha-gi.

692
00:51:28,807 --> 00:51:29,850
Don't be swayed.

693
00:51:55,834 --> 00:51:57,503
Here.

694
00:51:59,588 --> 00:52:01,715
The house must feel strange
to you, Jjak.

695
00:52:02,925 --> 00:52:04,635
This is where
you're going to stay for a while.

696
00:52:08,639 --> 00:52:11,099
I pretended to be fine

697
00:52:11,517 --> 00:52:13,185
but I was
actually very nervous today.

698
00:52:17,105 --> 00:52:19,024
I'm comfortable around Mr. Kang

699
00:52:19,733 --> 00:52:21,777
but why can't I do the same
with Chan?

700
00:52:24,404 --> 00:52:25,447
Right?

701
00:52:25,948 --> 00:52:27,824
Answer me, Jjak.

702
00:52:36,375 --> 00:52:38,961
Sounds good.
Then let's have dinner on Saturday.

703
00:52:39,044 --> 00:52:40,420
Okay.

704
00:52:52,182 --> 00:52:53,725
You look happy these days.

705
00:52:54,810 --> 00:52:57,813
Is it going well
with Da-reum or something?

706
00:53:00,065 --> 00:53:01,066
Cho-yi.

707
00:53:01,525 --> 00:53:03,360
Stop minding my private life

708
00:53:03,944 --> 00:53:05,612
and focus on your acting.

709
00:53:08,407 --> 00:53:09,658
Chan.

710
00:53:09,741 --> 00:53:12,578
Don't you know that any scandal
you get caught in affects me too?

711
00:53:14,621 --> 00:53:17,124
Stay low
until the show's over, will you?

712
00:53:20,669 --> 00:53:22,004
Just kidding.

713
00:53:22,087 --> 00:53:24,881
You wouldn't date your fan.

714
00:53:27,759 --> 00:53:30,304
- We're ready for the next scene.
- Okay.

715
00:53:34,516 --> 00:53:37,894
Let's go. We've got to love
each other beautifully again today.

716
00:54:04,671 --> 00:54:05,881
The woman of the day.

717
00:54:06,298 --> 00:54:10,010
This is for Ms. Nam Da-reum
who's in charge of the knot event.

718
00:54:10,594 --> 00:54:11,762
Get everything you want.

719
00:54:11,845 --> 00:54:13,597
Oh, I'm not in charge.

720
00:54:13,680 --> 00:54:15,474
I'm just the youngest member.

721
00:54:16,058 --> 00:54:19,019
It's not common for the youngest
to lead a big project like this.

722
00:54:19,102 --> 00:54:22,189
Everyone helped me.

723
00:54:22,439 --> 00:54:25,776
- Not to mention you, too.
- You're welcome.

724
00:54:26,318 --> 00:54:27,444
- Now, take a look.
- Okay.

725
00:54:34,117 --> 00:54:35,744
This is...

726
00:54:35,869 --> 00:54:37,537
It's not even English.

727
00:54:38,372 --> 00:54:39,665
What does it say?

728
00:54:39,956 --> 00:54:41,583
How come there are no pictures?

729
00:54:48,465 --> 00:54:51,718
- Are you ready?
- One second.

730
00:54:52,260 --> 00:54:55,681
- Do you need help?
- Oh, it's okay.

731
00:54:57,057 --> 00:54:59,476
It's not okay.

732
00:54:59,559 --> 00:55:01,186
Just ask him for help.

733
00:55:01,520 --> 00:55:03,063
Do you like fish or steak?

734
00:55:06,650 --> 00:55:09,277
I'm okay with anything.

735
00:55:11,988 --> 00:55:14,199
I like meat.

736
00:55:15,826 --> 00:55:17,035
Do you want me to order?

737
00:55:18,704 --> 00:55:19,788
Yes, please.

738
00:55:24,209 --> 00:55:25,627
We'll get the dinner course

739
00:55:25,711 --> 00:55:28,880
with bass and strip steak.

740
00:55:29,256 --> 00:55:31,883
Has the wine I asked for last time
been aerated?

741
00:55:31,967 --> 00:55:34,302
- Yes, I'll prepare it for you.
- Thank you.

742
00:55:37,889 --> 00:55:39,933
I ordered different dishes
so we can share.

743
00:55:40,016 --> 00:55:41,351
Sure. I'd love to.

744
00:55:48,316 --> 00:55:49,443
Hello.

745
00:55:49,860 --> 00:55:51,069
I made a reservation
under Kang Ha-gi.

746
00:55:51,862 --> 00:55:53,321
This way, please.

747
00:56:00,245 --> 00:56:01,788
This is a very nice restaurant.

748
00:56:04,750 --> 00:56:05,834
Ms. Da-reum?

749
00:56:23,602 --> 00:56:25,061
You must've been flustered last time.

750
00:56:25,937 --> 00:56:26,938
What?

751
00:56:27,606 --> 00:56:30,650
You had to leave
when my fans suddenly rushed over.

752
00:56:31,026 --> 00:56:32,110
I'm sorry.

753
00:56:35,447 --> 00:56:36,573
Don't mind it.

754
00:56:36,656 --> 00:56:39,659
They're all your fans just like me.

755
00:56:40,994 --> 00:56:42,078
I understand.

756
00:56:43,497 --> 00:56:44,539
Still...

757
00:56:46,708 --> 00:56:47,793
Da-reum

758
00:56:48,084 --> 00:56:49,544
you're different to me.

759
00:56:51,004 --> 00:56:52,297
Like I said last time

760
00:56:52,923 --> 00:56:54,424
I was able to endure
the hardest time of my life

761
00:56:55,008 --> 00:56:56,676
thanks to your photo book.

762
00:57:00,263 --> 00:57:01,389
Chan

763
00:57:02,182 --> 00:57:04,684
are you okay now?

764
00:57:05,727 --> 00:57:06,728
What do you mean?

765
00:57:09,439 --> 00:57:10,941
About having
a countless number of people

766
00:57:11,316 --> 00:57:13,318
who love you

767
00:57:13,777 --> 00:57:16,446
look for you,
and look forward to seeing you.

768
00:57:17,239 --> 00:57:18,657
Things like that.

769
00:57:20,992 --> 00:57:22,202
Do you want to know the truth?

770
00:57:28,750 --> 00:57:29,960
Sometimes it's tough.

771
00:57:31,127 --> 00:57:32,337
And it's overwhelming.

772
00:57:35,257 --> 00:57:36,633
As much as people love me

773
00:57:36,716 --> 00:57:39,261
I feel like I have to do well
and prove myself.

774
00:57:40,303 --> 00:57:43,473
I'm afraid one mistake would bring
everything down.

775
00:57:51,439 --> 00:57:53,984
WON-BIN

776
00:57:57,988 --> 00:58:00,782
Maybe something urgent came up.

777
00:58:01,575 --> 00:58:02,784
No, it's fine.

778
00:58:08,206 --> 00:58:09,875
COCOTALK

779
00:58:09,958 --> 00:58:11,877
Chan, it's urgent. Answer your phone.

780
00:58:13,461 --> 00:58:14,921
- Chan.
- Yes.

781
00:58:15,005 --> 00:58:16,631
Why weren't you answering your phone?

782
00:58:16,715 --> 00:58:18,341
I'm outside right now.

783
00:58:18,967 --> 00:58:20,051
What's up?

784
00:58:20,760 --> 00:58:23,930
Director Park Chan-dong
gave us a call.

785
00:58:24,347 --> 00:58:26,391
He wants to see you
at his studio right now.

786
00:58:26,474 --> 00:58:27,976
I guess he liked you at the audition.

787
00:58:28,143 --> 00:58:29,227
Really?

788
00:58:34,024 --> 00:58:35,400
But not now.

789
00:58:37,485 --> 00:58:38,737
This is more important.

790
00:58:38,820 --> 00:58:40,196
Hey. Are you nuts?

791
00:58:40,280 --> 00:58:41,656
This is
a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.

792
00:58:41,907 --> 00:58:44,576
This could get you to Cannes.

793
00:58:45,035 --> 00:58:47,162
No more nonsense. Wrap it up now.

794
00:58:47,537 --> 00:58:48,997
I'll go pick you up now.

795
00:59:05,180 --> 00:59:06,890
Da-reum, I'm sorry...

796
00:59:09,726 --> 00:59:11,102
Do you have to go?

797
00:59:11,186 --> 00:59:13,396
A meeting just got scheduled
for my next project.

798
00:59:14,397 --> 00:59:16,399
That's really important.

799
00:59:16,483 --> 00:59:19,152
The director's only available
right now.

800
00:59:19,235 --> 00:59:20,236
I'm sorry.

801
00:59:20,445 --> 00:59:22,822
Oh, no. It's okay.

802
00:59:23,239 --> 00:59:24,574
Like you said earlier

803
00:59:24,824 --> 00:59:27,202
you have to prove yourself
as much as you're loved.

804
00:59:27,702 --> 00:59:28,954
Sorry about this, Da-reum.

805
00:59:30,246 --> 00:59:32,874
It's really okay.
You should get going.

806
00:59:33,416 --> 00:59:35,335
- I'll call you.
- Yes.

807
00:59:39,631 --> 00:59:40,632
Go on.

808
01:00:29,472 --> 01:00:32,267
Your party
had arranged this in advance.

809
01:00:47,449 --> 01:00:49,284
MS. NAM DA-REUM
HAPPY BIRTHDAY

810
01:00:52,078 --> 01:00:53,246
What's she doing alone?

811
01:00:53,955 --> 01:00:56,207
She's looking this way.

812
01:00:56,374 --> 01:00:59,210
That's sad.

813
01:01:00,795 --> 01:01:02,714
HAPPY BIRTHDAY TO NAM DA-REUM

814
01:01:13,516 --> 01:01:15,810
Wait, no one showed up for real?

815
01:01:15,894 --> 01:01:17,312
LEE YE-JI

816
01:01:17,854 --> 01:01:18,855
Sorry.

817
01:01:19,105 --> 01:01:21,441
Hey. I told you. That place is lame.

818
01:01:21,524 --> 01:01:23,318
The master of playing by herself.

819
01:01:23,401 --> 01:01:25,612
Nam Da-reum's
legendary solo birthday party.

820
01:01:34,954 --> 01:01:37,457
Are your friends running late?

821
01:01:39,709 --> 01:01:40,877
They'll be here soon.

822
01:01:42,003 --> 01:01:43,129
It's okay.

823
01:02:11,324 --> 01:02:12,367
Mr. Kang.

824
01:02:13,409 --> 01:02:15,411
- Get up.
- Sorry?

825
01:02:30,176 --> 01:02:31,177
Ms. Nam.

826
01:02:33,054 --> 01:02:34,139
Have you been

827
01:02:35,807 --> 01:02:37,142
going on blind dates by any chance?

828
01:02:37,684 --> 01:02:39,519
Blind dates?

829
01:02:39,853 --> 01:02:41,396
Last time, when you asked me
to watch the cats

830
01:02:42,522 --> 01:02:43,606
and even today.

831
01:02:45,316 --> 01:02:46,317
Oh, right.

832
01:02:46,651 --> 01:02:48,361
Yes, it's a blind date.

833
01:02:49,154 --> 01:02:51,114
If you're trying to get over
someone you like

834
01:02:52,782 --> 01:02:53,783
don't bother.

835
01:02:55,785 --> 01:02:56,953
You don't need

836
01:02:58,288 --> 01:02:59,664
to let go of your feelings.

837
01:03:01,749 --> 01:03:03,793
Okay.

838
01:03:05,044 --> 01:03:07,005
Anyway, did he leave without you?

839
01:03:09,215 --> 01:03:10,300
Well...

840
01:03:11,134 --> 01:03:13,720
I was kind of flustered too.

841
01:03:14,470 --> 01:03:16,681
But it happens.

842
01:03:19,434 --> 01:03:21,978
- I'm okay.
- But you're not.

843
01:03:24,981 --> 01:03:26,191
You always say

844
01:03:27,275 --> 01:03:28,318
you're okay.

845
01:03:30,153 --> 01:03:32,155
I guess people won't feel as bad
when you say that.

846
01:03:33,448 --> 01:03:34,949
But you're hurt.

847
01:03:36,534 --> 01:03:37,660
At least, in front of me

848
01:03:39,871 --> 01:03:41,206
you can say it's not okay.

849
01:03:48,213 --> 01:03:49,214
Okay.

850
01:03:50,506 --> 01:03:51,507
To be honest

851
01:03:53,426 --> 01:03:54,719
it wasn't okay.

852
01:03:56,638 --> 01:03:57,805
It's okay.

853
01:04:01,226 --> 01:04:03,102
When I pretend to be okay

854
01:04:07,732 --> 01:04:08,733
I look

855
01:04:10,985 --> 01:04:12,654
less pitiful.

856
01:04:14,864 --> 01:04:17,492
"I'm really fine."

857
01:04:19,911 --> 01:04:22,163
It's really okay.
You should get going.

858
01:04:26,751 --> 01:04:28,628
I've always swallowed it.

859
01:04:30,672 --> 01:04:33,258
But today, it kind of hurts.

860
01:04:33,841 --> 01:04:35,510
Don't meet anyone like that.

861
01:04:38,304 --> 01:04:39,389
Ms. Nam Da-reum.

862
01:04:40,014 --> 01:04:41,557
You deserve better than that.

863
01:04:43,476 --> 01:04:47,146
You don't deserve to date a jerk

864
01:04:48,564 --> 01:04:49,857
who leaves you on a blind date.

865
01:04:58,741 --> 01:05:01,911
That jerk is your friend.

866
01:05:03,204 --> 01:05:04,247
Why are you smiling?

867
01:05:08,042 --> 01:05:10,044
No, it's nothing.

868
01:05:15,383 --> 01:05:17,927
Maybe something more important
than me came up.

869
01:05:19,679 --> 01:05:21,389
Still, for some reason

870
01:05:22,473 --> 01:05:23,766
it's less disappointing today.

871
01:05:24,851 --> 01:05:26,853
Perhaps because I'm walking with you.

872
01:05:29,397 --> 01:05:30,648
I think

873
01:05:31,816 --> 01:05:33,234
I feel better.

874
01:05:33,943 --> 01:05:35,236
The air is nice.

875
01:05:38,031 --> 01:05:39,782
This is a lot better
than the blind date.

876
01:05:47,248 --> 01:05:48,541
I should go home

877
01:05:50,168 --> 01:05:51,377
but I don't want to.

878
01:05:52,045 --> 01:05:53,087
Why not?

879
01:05:56,841 --> 01:05:57,842
Because

880
01:06:00,094 --> 01:06:01,763
I want to stay like this.

881
01:06:03,056 --> 01:06:04,098
Sorry?

882
01:06:07,310 --> 01:06:08,478
Because of Kung.

883
01:06:09,228 --> 01:06:11,647
He doesn't stop running at night
as if he's possessed.

884
01:06:13,191 --> 01:06:14,359
Jjak too.

885
01:06:15,318 --> 01:06:18,321
Apparently, when they're kittens,
they have too much energy to handle.

886
01:06:18,738 --> 01:06:21,532
If Jjak doesn't sleep during the day,
he runs so much at dawn.

887
01:06:21,616 --> 01:06:23,493
So I keep waking up at dawn.

888
01:06:23,868 --> 01:06:26,162
If they live together,
it'll be war every day.

889
01:06:27,163 --> 01:06:28,206
But then

890
01:06:28,664 --> 01:06:31,209
if they stay together,
they'll be less lonely.

891
01:06:36,839 --> 01:06:38,174
This is Jjak from earlier today.

892
01:06:38,508 --> 01:06:41,135
He was enjoying the sunlight,
then he dozed off.

893
01:06:41,677 --> 01:06:43,012
Just like the owner.

894
01:06:43,763 --> 01:06:46,057
So bright and gentle.

895
01:07:01,489 --> 01:07:03,366
It's the first snow this season.

896
01:07:05,576 --> 01:07:06,828
It's pretty.

897
01:07:12,834 --> 01:07:13,876
Yes.

898
01:07:15,920 --> 01:07:17,088
So pretty.

899
01:07:57,712 --> 01:08:01,424
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

900
01:08:11,642 --> 01:08:13,895
Do you want to meet outside?

901
01:08:14,353 --> 01:08:17,106
How can Mr. Kang be fine?

902
01:08:17,190 --> 01:08:18,524
He's such a pro.

903
01:08:18,941 --> 01:08:21,194
To be honest... Wait!

904
01:08:21,277 --> 01:08:24,113
I liked him for a very long time.

905
01:08:24,489 --> 01:08:25,531
LA?

906
01:08:25,615 --> 01:08:26,949
Why don't you come with me?

907
01:08:27,116 --> 01:08:28,576
Whoever he is

908
01:08:28,659 --> 01:08:30,953
you don't need to put up
with him that much.

909
01:08:31,037 --> 01:08:32,747
Are you protecting your employee

910
01:08:32,830 --> 01:08:33,956
or are you keeping me in check?

911
01:08:34,749 --> 01:08:36,918
Mr. Kang, the truth is...

912
01:08:37,251 --> 01:08:38,961
- Is this...
- Chan, where are you going?

913
01:08:39,170 --> 01:08:40,296
Is this true?
